### Page 5 of 7

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
March 4, 2025
Resolutions
15. Consideration of a resolution designating the Cheyenne America 250
Commission as the official Laramie County America 250
Commission.
25 - 090
Resolution, Cheyenne America 250 Commission
Attachments:
Nathaniel Trelease, chairman of the Cheyenne America 250 Commission, said the
resolution will enable the Commission to apply for and secure grant funding from a
state appropriation specifically allocated for events and activities celebrating the
250th anniversary of United States Declaration of Independence.  He said a number
of activities are planned to commemorate the historic milestone.
A motion was made by Commissioner Zwonitzer, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, that this agenda item be approved. The motion
carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Zwonitzer
Aye:
Hollingshead
Excused:
16. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a request for the vacation of Rd 103
described as commencing at the intersection of Rd 239 and running
thence north approximately 165 ft through Sect 3, T18N, R70W of the
6th PM and Sects 34, 33, and 28, T19N, R70W of the 6th PM,
Laramie County, WY, and terminating at the north line of Sect 28,
contiguous to Sect 21, T19N, R70W of the 6th PM, Laramie County,
WY.
25 - 092
Resolution, Rd 103, RP#512
Attachments:
Molly Bennett, Public Works, reported that the viewer, Scott Larson, recommended
approval of the vacation.  She stated that no objections or claims for damages were
received during the public notice period.  Chairman Malm opened the hearing for
PUBLIC COMMENT.  Hearing no PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the
hearing.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, that this agenda item be approved. The motion
carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Zwonitzer
Aye:
Hollingshead
Excused:
Grants
17. Consideration of an agreement between Laramie County, WY, and
Great Western Installation in the amount of $201,221.53 to provide
and install playground equipment at North Clear Creek Park.
25 - 091
